_reason":null,"evidence":["outbound_mutation_builders.py:225 calls note_absent_or_rekey, not note_absent directly","binding_store.py:435-440: `if client is None or not jira_id: self.note_absent(...)` else `_current_key_by_id(client, jira_id)` then note_absent on decline","_current_key_by_id (binding_store.py:97-118) calls client.get_issue_by_rest(jira_id) — a numeric id, not the key","dispatch_one.py:233-235 captures jira_id via record_jira_id(local_id, result.get('id','')); the plan-described fake create_issue returns {'key': key} with NO 'id', so record_jira_id is a no-op and jira_id stays falsy — the ONLY reason the rekey branch is skipped today","Plan Test 2 text: '`DIG-1` out-of-window AND deleted -> the direct GET 404s -> `note_absent`(-or-rekey) records the absence' — silent on the jira_id/rekey precondition"],"finding":"Test 2's route to note_absent depends on an unstated fact: absence bookkeeping runs through the note_absent_or_rekey coordinator, which re-asks by numeric jira_id (client.get_issue_by_rest(jira_id)) before recording absence and only degrades to note_absent when jira_id is falsy. The plan's Test 2 describes only a direct-GET 404 on 'deleted' keys and never states (a) that it relies on the binding having no captured jira_id, nor (b) how the fake's get_issue_by_rest must behave when called with an ID (not a key) argument.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcc6b28a9ea6e4e58","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — Test 2 (test_out_of_window_404_then_alive_roundtrip_clears_absence); Harness bullet '_FakeJiraState ... get_issue_by_rest raises HTTPError(404) for deleted keys'","norm_id":"n0da97404434f6df4","priority":0.495,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future harness edit adds 'id' to the fake's create_issue return to be more faithful: note_absent_or_rekey then calls get_issue_by_rest(<numeric id>); the fake 404s only on deleted KEYS, so the id lookup's outcome is unspecified and Test 2 may take the rekey branch (or resolve alive) instead of note_absent — silently invalidating the counter-rise assertion"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In the Test 2 description and the harness spec, add: 'note_absent is reached via the note_absent_or_rekey coordinator, which re-asks by numeric jira_id; the fake create_issue omits id so no jira_id is captured and the seam degrades straight to note_absent. Either keep that invariant (and assert it) or have the fake get_issue_by_rest 404 on the numeric id too, and assert DIG-1's key is unchanged (rekey branch not taken).'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":nul